course: dictionary
lesson: 1975
title: Complex: many connected parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Complex is an adjective meaning made of many connected parts, and hard to understand or explain. Read «they had some of the first complex eyes, made of crystal». Do the eyes sound simple, or do they have many parts? The words made of crystal help you see that complex means having many parts.
explain: Complex can also be a noun. A complex is a group of buildings used for one purpose, as in «a sports complex». A complex can also be a strong, worried feeling, as in «He has a complex about his height». In science, a complex is a group of things that work together.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap your meaning into the sentence and check it. Does «the eyes were made of many connected parts» make sense? Does «a group of buildings» fit the sports word? The sentence tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Complex means made of many connected parts and hard to understand or explain.
fact: A complex is a group of buildings used for one purpose, as in «a sports complex».
fact: A complex is a strong, worried feeling, as in «He has a complex about his height».
fact: In grammar, a complex sentence has a main clause and a subordinate clause.
fact: Trilobites were sea creatures with jointed legs and hard shells, and they lived for about 270 million years.
exercise: In «some of the first complex eyes, made of crystal», what does complex mean? | Simple and plain | Wet and slippery | *Made of many connected parts | Very fast
exercise: In «a sports complex», what is a complex? | A sea creature | *A group of buildings used for one purpose | A worried feeling | A kind of sports shoe
exercise: Which of these is a complex sentence? | Ben, Sam and Tom ran | Ben and Sam ran fast | Ben ran fast | *Ben ran because he was late
test: What does complex mean in «a complex problem with many steps»? | Easy and quick | A kind of sea creature | *Having many connected parts and hard to explain | A group of buildings
test: Which phrase uses complex to mean a group of buildings? | Complex eyes made of crystal | A complex sentence | A complex about his height | *A sports complex
exam: Which sentence shows that complex means a worried feeling? | *He has a complex about his height | The trilobite had complex eyes | The sports complex opens at nine | The apartment complex is very big
